From d9081448e378afbdd07708a3659fc59a7de5d2a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Tridgell <andrew@tridgell.net>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 17:13:13 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 03/12] brush-loss, brush-train: numeric targets and hot-pixel
 weighted L1

The loss kernels read float targets (f32 bits, opaque, same value for every
channel) when ImageLossConfig.float_gt is set, and weight the L1 term of
pixels whose target exceeds hot_threshold by 1 + hot_weight (forward and
backward). New training options --hot-weight (default 0, off) and
--hot-threshold. Eval of numeric targets skips the 8-bit round trip, clamps
to [0, 1] and saves renders as 16-bit gray (value * 65535).
---
